CONTEXT="""One complete wristband-for-bow exchange. Lil greets Hodram, boasts about the displayed bow as this region's Proof of Supremacy, and resists handing it over casually. Hodram's silence gives her room to propose one particular trade. She excitedly names the Heavenly Wristband and reports an indefinite New World location, offering the bow if it is found and brought back. A possession-related path has her ask to see the wristband, delight in its cuteness and request it in exchange for the bow. The two player options are agreement and refusal. Her disbelief at refusal leads to Hodram's quiet negated denial of disinterest, a renewed reciprocal demand and delighted farewell. Keep the other celebratory farewell distinct. The FE notice reports the outgoing wristband. Preserve eight original relative sites and both options; native UI result routing and actual eligibility/path activation remain separate checks. Original event49 requires48, whose earlier dialogue instructs the addressee to wait in Amsterdam; this does not independently prove B49's original location or outer scheduler conditions. Do not add a rank, relationship, cash price, item power, exact New World location or extra reward."""
DECISIONS={
6:('retention',"You're here!",'The short exclamation is natural, eager recognition of the arriving addressee. It carries the clean repeated きたきた greeting in Lil\'s casual voice without inventing lateness, impatience or a prior appointment. The next line supplies her playful bargaining; no extra greeting is needed.'),
10:('revision',"Heh-heh. It's this region's Proof of Supremacy, you know. I can't just hand it over!",'Restore Lil\'s self-satisfied laugh and the object\'s regional Proof identity. Use the already reviewed project term Proof of Supremacy for 覇者の証/しるし. I can\'t just hand it over preserves reluctance to give it up easily; So no, it\'s not yours wrongly turns that bargaining into a flat denial. The following offer shows that she is willing to trade. This identifies the quest object rather than inventing a political office or territorial conquest.'),
15:('retention','…','The clean source explicitly gives Hodram a wordless ellipsis. The current single ellipsis preserves his restrained reaction and the beat before Lil introduces her trade. Keep the source-proven glyph; add no spoken agreement, annoyance, motive or relationship.'),
19:('revision',"But there's one thing I'd trade it for.",'State the actual proposal: there is one particular object she would accept in exchange. Might change my mind is a vague change of attitude and loses the explicit trade. The contraction and straightforward phrasing fit Lil\'s quick, informal sales pitch.'),
22:('revision',"It's called a Heavenly Wristband or something. It's super cute!",'Keep the established item84 name. Lil\'s phonetic てんゆー title and とかいって give the name a casual, approximate presentation; or something conveys that informality without changing the identified object. Super cute carries ちょーキュート as ordinary enthusiastic American speech. Restore the name-introduction and her excitement rather than leaving a pair of compressed label fragments. Add no magic, stats, rarity or deity.'),
33:('revision',"I hear it's somewhere in the New World. Find it and bring it back, and I'll give you this. Bye-bye!",'Retain hearsay and restore the indefinite somewhere, finding it, bringing it back and the conditional exchange offer. This line explicitly promises this object if the wristband is brought, unlike B48\'s earlier wait instruction. Bye-bye carries her breezy, drawn-out farewell. Do not add an exact town, island, guaranteed find or unconditional player award.'),
40:('retention','You already have it? Let me see!','The surprised question and eager request are natural in the complete possession-related exchange. Already expresses her surprise that the requested item is on hand; it does not claim that a particular voyage has happened. One enthusiastic Let me see carries the repeated Japanese request without losing its purpose. The following delighted reaction supplies the emotional escalation.'),
43:('revision',"Wow! It really is cute! Hey, give it to me! I'll give you this bow!",'Restore her delighted confirmation, direct request and reciprocal bow offer as spoken dialogue. Take the bow; give me that is an abrupt semicolon instruction that flattens her excitement and the offer before the choice. This bow refers to the single identified item148, whose established English asset is Ullr\'s Bow; the Japanese 弓矢 does not authorize promising a separate inventory award. Keep wristband-to-Lil/bow-to-addressee direction and leave the player\'s options intact.'),
58:('retention','Yes! No changing your mind! See you!','These are idiomatic, buoyant exclamations for Lil\'s successful bargaining. No changing your mind preserves her playful insistence that the agreement stand; See you keeps the quick farewell. It adds no threat, permanent oath or gameplay restriction.'),
64:('retention',"What?! Don't you want the Proof?",'The disbelieving exclamation and direct question work naturally after refusal. The Proof recalls the regional Proof of Supremacy explicitly introduced earlier, preserving the persuasive object identity without repeating the full name. Keep it as a question: the next line qualifies the apparent refusal. Add no declaration that Hodram has no interest.'),
67:('revision',"…It's not that I don't want it.",'Restore the source\'s negated denial of disinterest. The bow matters substitutes a different assertion and loses the hesitation that Lil immediately uses to press the trade. The quiet ellipsis and deliberately qualified reply suit Hodram\'s restraint. It is neither a blunt refusal nor an explicit enthusiastic acceptance.'),
71:('retention','Exactly! Here, take this. Now give me the wristband!','Exactly picks up Hodram\'s qualification, and the paired imperatives preserve Lil\'s pushy, playful reciprocity. The explicit wristband clarifies the source demonstrative using the already identified trade object. Here and Now fit the immediate exchange without inventing grabbing, theft, payment or affection.'),
74:('retention','Wow! So cute! Yes! Bye!','The quick exclamations are natural spontaneous delight, a celebratory Yes and a brisk farewell. Keep this later ending distinct from the earlier matching Japanese opening: it has no renewed request or bow offer. Short fragments suit the source excitement here; they are not retained to meet an allocation limit.'),
81:('revision','You handed over the Heavenly Wristband.','Use a clear, natural completed-action notice. Heavenly Wristband given is telegraphic and can read like an incoming item notification. The clean を渡しました reports the outgoing wristband, so make the player-facing direction explicit. Preserve the original unvoiced FE system consumer; do not assign actor254, name a personal speaker, report bow receipt or invent extra effects.'),
48:('retention','All right.','This is a composed, natural affirmative choice for いいだろう in Hodram\'s voice. It agrees to the proposed trade without adding enthusiasm, a relationship or a new promise. Retain the exact wording; the typed-table compiler owns terminators and alignment.'),
50:('retention','No.','This direct, restrained refusal is natural for だめだ and sets up Lil\'s disbelief and Hodram\'s later qualification. Preserve No. as the logical label. The three current trailing spaces are storage padding, not authored dialogue; removing them during typed-table compilation changes layout storage rather than the words or editorial decision.'),
}
